From: Rasheed <99349713+gitRasheed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:31:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/61] NNS.caus: orient the p.value statistic as x -> y

With p.value = TRUE the observed and permutation statistics came from
signed_from_cp(), which returned cp[3] without looking at its name. cp[3]
is the log-ratio in the direction of the stronger causation, labelled
"C(x--->y)" or "C(y--->x)", and is non-negative in practice, so the
'signed' x -> y statistic ignored direction: NNS.caus(x, y) and
NNS.caus(y, x) reported the same observed_signed and the same
x_causes_y p-value. Flip the sign for "C(y--->x)", as NNS.caus.matrix
already does.

Evidence (x ~ N(0,1), y = x^2 + N(0,0.1^2), n = 300, nperm = 50, seed 1):
  NNS.caus(x, y): C(x--->y) 1.428, observed_signed 1.428,
                  p x_causes_y 0.0196, p y_causes_x 1       (unchanged)
  NNS.caus(y, x): C(y--->x) 1.428
    before: observed_signed  1.428, p x_causes_y 0.0196, p y_causes_x 1
    after:  observed_signed -1.428, p x_causes_y 1,      p y_causes_x 0.0196

The causation vector itself is unchanged; the p-values, observed_signed,
null_distribution and CI change whenever a statistic is labelled
C(y--->x).
---
 R/Uni_Causation.R | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/R/Uni_Causation.R b/R/Uni_Causation.R
index 5bbd662..401b583 100644
--- a/R/Uni_Causation.R
+++ b/R/Uni_Causation.R
@@ -95,10 +95,13 @@ Uni.caus <- function(x, y, tau, plot = TRUE){
 
 
 
-# Internal helper: extract canonical signed causation from the third element of cp.
+# Internal helper: extract canonical signed causation x -> y from cp.
 signed_from_cp <- function(cp){
-  # Extract the third element (log-ratio in direction of stronger causation) and cap infinities
+  # The third element is the log-ratio in the direction of the stronger
+  # causation; its name carries the direction. Orient it as x -> y (flip the
+  # sign for "C(y--->x)", as NNS.caus.matrix does) and cap infinities.
   raw_val <- as.numeric(cp[3])
+  if(identical(names(cp)[3], "C(y--->x)")) raw_val <- -raw_val
   if(is.infinite(raw_val)) raw_val <- sign(raw_val) * 100
   return(raw_val)
 }
